        "body": "Attach the escalation playbook and the rehearsal scenario to the case, label their versions, and record the time each was observed. Preserve a conflicting value instead of overwriting the first one. The next reviewer should not have to ask which document is authoritative. Mark missing evidence as missing, with a reason, rather than leaving a blank. A sample client escalation rehearsal review checks the escalation playbook, the rehearsal scenario, and the surviving value in the operational record.\n\nA clean-looking status is not evidence that the underlying work is correct. Record who supplied each document and when it arrived. Link each value to the field or page that supports it. The record should show the source, the decision, and the surviving value in one place. Apply the same client escalation rehearsal test to the participant list and to the value that survives in the operational record.\n\nA case that moves between owners should keep both owner periods visible. If the team cannot reproduce the result from the record, the control is not finished. Keep the original request so a later correction does not erase the reason for the work. A clean-looking status is not evidence that the underlying work is correct. A client escalation rehearsal exception keeps the lessons record attached and routes the question to the operations lead."
